{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Replacing a hand-written registry","modules":[{"name":"LinkerSets"}]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/Performance"],"generated":true,"title":"Guides"}],"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A registry is a list someone has to keep in step with the code: every analytics event type in an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"array, every route in a table, every dependency registered in one function at startup. A new type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that isn’t added works everywhere except where the list is read, and nothing tells you. Moving the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"list onto LinkerSets takes four steps, and the list is deleted at the end.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Take an analytics library whose events are types conforming to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsEvent"},{"type":"text","text":", collected by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hand so the library can validate their schemas at launch:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public protocol AnalyticsEvent {","    static var name: String { get }","}","","\/\/ Every module's events, listed by hand.","let allEvents: [any AnalyticsEvent.Type] = [","    Login.self,","    Logout.self,","    PurchaseCompleted.self,","]"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"1. Give the library a macro","type":"heading","anchor":"1-Give-the-library-a-macro"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick a kind (“evnt” is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0x6576_6E74"},{"type":"text","text":", as "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind"},{"type":"text","text":" explains) and add a compiler plugin"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose macro requires the protocol, so its records hold "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"any AnalyticsEvent.Type"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public enum EventMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x6576_6E74 }  \/\/ \"evnt\"","","    public static func requiredConformance(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> TypeSyntax? {","        \"Analytics.AnalyticsEvent\"","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The library declares the macro and the kind, re-exports LinkerSets for the expansion, and reads"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the set for its users:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@_exported import LinkerSets","","extension LinkerSetKind {","    static let events = LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x6576_6E74)  \/\/ \"evnt\"","}","","@attached(peer)","public macro Event() = #externalMacro(module: \"AnalyticsMacros\", type: \"EventMacro\")","","public enum AnalyticsEvents {","    public static var all: [any AnalyticsEvent.Type] {","        LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>(kind: .events).values","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The re-export is required. The expansion lands in each user’s file and calls LinkerSets’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#linkerSetRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" there, so that file must see the LinkerSets module. A library that imports"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"LinkerSets without re-exporting it leaves its users’ files failing with “no macro named"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"‘linkerSetRecord’” unless each one imports LinkerSets too. The re-export also puts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSet"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSetKind"},{"type":"text","text":" in scope wherever the library is imported. Keep the kind"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"internal and hand users the values through the library’s own API ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsEvents.all"},{"type":"text","text":"), so the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"set is read in one place."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The LinkerSetsMacroSupport module’s documentation has the package targets this needs."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"2. Read the set beside the list","type":"heading","anchor":"2-Read-the-set-beside-the-list"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Before touching any event, read both and compare them, in a test or a debug build:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let discovered = AnalyticsEvents.all","let missing = allEvents.filter { listed in !discovered.contains { $0 == listed } }"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"missing","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" starts as the whole list and shrinks as events are marked."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"3. Mark each event where it’s declared","type":"heading","anchor":"3-Mark-each-event-where-its-declared"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@Event","struct Login: AnalyticsEvent {","    static let name = \"login\"","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An event that doesn’t conform fails to compile. A generic event type, or one nested in a generic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type, is refused with a message, as "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse"},{"type":"text","text":" lists; such a type needs its concrete"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specializations listed by hand, or a concrete wrapper."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"4. Delete the list","type":"heading","anchor":"4-Delete-the-list"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Once ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"missing"},{"text":" is empty, the library reads the set instead:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let allEvents = LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>(kind: .events).values"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"and the hand-written array goes. A new event is registered by writing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":" on it, in whichever"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"module declares it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Other registries","type":"heading","anchor":"Other-registries"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The same steps fit any list whose entries can be declared as constants, functions or types:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Routes","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Route static let profile = Route(path: \"\/profile\")","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", read as ","type":"text"},{"code":"LinkerSet<Route>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Migrations","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Migration static func addUsers(_ db: inout Database)"},{"type":"text","text":", read as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSet<(inout Database) -> Void>"},{"type":"text","text":", sorted by a version the migration declares."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Dependency registrations"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Registration static func register(_ container: Container)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"module registering its own factories, read and called once at startup.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A registry whose order matters gets it from the entries, never from the set: the linker’s order is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stable but not one you choose ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Move a central list of event types, routes or registrations onto declarations that find"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"themselves."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersets\/replacingaregistry"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/WhatTheMacrosRefuse":{"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/whatthemacrosrefuse","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Every declaration a record can’t describe is a compile error, with a message that says why.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","title":"What the macros refuse","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/DeclaringAKind":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick the number that tags your declarations, and decide whether your users write it."}],"title":"Declaring a kind","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/declaringakind"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/FindingRecords":{"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/findingrecords","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Read every declaration of a kind, as the type you expect."}],"kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Finding records","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/PlatformsAndLinking":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where records are found, how, and which test shows it."}],"title":"Platforms and linking","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/platformsandlinking"},"doc://LinkerSetsRuntime/documentation/LinkerSetsRuntime/LinkerSetKind":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tag that says which client a linker-set record belongs to."}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsruntime\/linkersetkind","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSetKind","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LinkerSetKind","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"LinkerSetKind","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"LinkerSetKind","type":"topic"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Declarations that register themselves at compile time and are found at run time across every module a program links.","type":"text"}],"title":"LinkerSets","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets"},"doc://LinkerSetsRuntime/documentation/LinkerSetsRuntime/LinkerSet":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every record of one kind, across every image the program has loaded, and the values they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"produce."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsruntime\/linkerset","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinkerSet"}],"title":"LinkerSet","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinkerSet"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSet"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/Performance":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What records cost as an app grows: nothing at launch, a walk of the records when a set is read,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a few milliseconds of build time per marked declaration."}],"title":"Performance","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/Performance","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/performance"}}}